      "text": "We first find the vector passing through $(2,2,1)$ and $(5,1,-2).$\nThis vector is given by $\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\-1\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}.$\nThen, we use the point $4$ in $2$ on the vector to find the $z$-coordinate.\n\nOur point is $z$ on the line through $(2,2,1)$ and $(5,1,-2).$ Therefore the $z$-coordinate of this point is of the form $z=z_{1}+n\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-1\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix},$ where $n$ is an integer.\nPlugging in $2,2,$ and $1+3n$ into the expression for z, we have $2=4-z_{1},$\nand $2=-1(2)+1+3n,$ where $n$ is an integer.\nSolving these equations, we have $z_{1}=2,$ and $n=1.$\nThus the answer is $\\boxed{2}$. The answer is \\boxed{2}.",
